hints.body:
Write a type guard function:
```typescript
function isUser(data: unknown): data is User {
  return (
    typeof data === 'object' &&
    data !== null &&
    typeof (data as Record<string, unknown>).id === 'string' &&
    typeof (data as Record<string, unknown>).email === 'string' &&
    typeof (data as Record<string, unknown>).name === 'string'
  );
}
```
Then in `loadUser`, replace the bare `as User` with:
```typescript
if (!isUser(data)) throw new Error('API returned invalid user shape');
const user = data;  // now narrowed to User by the guard
```
This way, malformed API responses are caught immediately with a clear error, instead of a confusing `TypeError` several lines later.
